change:
  id: CHG-015
  title: Make independent review and consolidation part of the operating contract
  status: proposed
  intent: Record how independent review fans out and how findings are consolidated, in the framework template so generated projects inherit it and in this project's AGENTS.md with a guard so it cannot silently drift.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - PAT-003
    - PAT-002
    - LRN-001
    - ARCH-001

deltas:
  - op: ADDED
    capability: review-and-consolidation-contract
    requirement: The operating contract states that reviews may fan out, that implementation agents may not share a file, and that consolidation is deduplicate, adjudicate, verify then apply serially.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: the repository contract is checked
        then: AGENTS.md carries an independent review and consolidation section naming every load-bearing control
        and:
          - deleting any one control fails the check and names it
      - id: S2
        when: a project is generated from the framework template
        then: its required-section list includes independent review and consolidation, stated generally rather than with this project's examples
      - id: S3
        when: an agent consults the knowledge graph about review practice
        then: PAT-003 records the pattern with the concrete incidents that produced it, and links to PAT-002 for reviewer session hygiene and LRN-001 for recovering a review believed lost

acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: repo-contract/agents-review-consolidation-controls
    layer: contract
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: manual/agents-template-required-sections
    layer: contract
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: repo-contract/knowledge-pat-003-resolves
    layer: contract

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: add the required section to the framework AGENTS template, stated generally
    status: completed
  - id: T2
    slice: add the section to this project's AGENTS.md, which CLAUDE.md symlinks
    status: completed
  - id: T3
    slice: guard the section's controls in check-repo-contract so deleting one fails and names it
    status: completed
  - id: T4
    slice: record PAT-003 with the incidents that produced it
    status: completed

non_goals:
  - automating reviewer dispatch or consolidation
  - changing how any specific reviewer is invoked
  - anything touching the deterministic decision boundary

risks:
  - a contract that says reviews may fan out could be read as licence to spawn reviewers freely; the cost is consolidation, which is serial and falls on the lead, so the section says consolidation is the work rather than the reviewing
  - PAT-003 is proposed rather than canonical because it generalises from one day's incidents and was written by the actor involved in them
